  "name": "Lucky Bastard Box: Mundane",
  "img": "icons/svg/d20-grey.svg",
  "description": "<p>A Lucky Bastard Box's mundane - good-luck charms and gambling prizes (p.22). Drawn for the one item of a Bronze box when the box's title names the theme (\"Bronze Lucky Bastard Box\"; module/helpers/loot.mjs boxTableNames). A \"&lt;Tier&gt; Lucky Bastard Box: Mundane\" table, if a GM makes one, comes first. A row's name can set a quantity - \"Torch ×10\", \"Bandages (1d6)\" - and a text row becomes a simple item of that name, its description the row's. Edit a copy in the world's Roll Tables (or a world compendium) to change what a box holds.</p>",
